qfappd (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix block enforcement: NF_ACCEPT verdicts reinject at the next forward
    hook, skipping the rest of the queueing base chain, so the persist and
    block rules placed there never ran — verdicts were computed and logged
    but nothing was ever dropped. They now live in a second forward base
    chain (`forward_verdict`, priority filter + 20) that reinjected packets
    do traverse.
  * qfappd-apply now writes /run/qfappd/apply.json (ok/error + the desired
    file's mtime/size) so the WebUI can surface refused desired states and
    saved-but-never-applied policies — previously a check-policy failure
    left the old policy enforced with no indication anywhere.
  * Fix the apply trigger dying permanently: PathExists= in the .path unit
    re-triggered the oneshot in a loop whenever it ran (the file always
    exists), hitting the start-rate limit and failing BOTH units with
    unit-start-limit-hit — after which WebUI saves were silently never
    published. The watcher now uses PathChanged only (matching the IPS
    module); the boot-time initial publish moves to the apply service
    itself (WantedBy=multi-user.target), and the apply service sets
    StartLimitIntervalSec=0 so bursts of saves cannot kill the watcher.

 -- QuartzFire <cwellman@quartz.systems>  Sat, 11 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000

qfappd (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: nDPI-based Application Control for QuartzFire.
    - Named actions with per-application / per-category allow-block verdicts.
    - Per-firewall-rule bindings via ct-mark ACTION_ID.
    - NFQUEUE classification with conntrack-mark fast-path offload.
    - gRPC introspection API + JSON event stream.

 -- QuartzFire <cwellman@quartz.systems>  Sat, 11 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
